<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Crécy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1346">1346</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Crécy · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Crécy was fought on 26 August 1346 near Crécy-en-Ponthieu in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a>, in a defensive position, defeated a much larger French army under Philip VI, as English and Welsh longbowmen broke repeated French cavalry charges. Many French nobles died, among them the blind <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, and Edward went on to besiege Calais.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-crecy.jpg" alt="Battle of Crécy" width="320" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Loyset Liédet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_crecy_froissart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
